  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::9132",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to interact with multiple potassium channel proteins, including Kcna6, Kcnf1, and Kcnv2, all of which are involved in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the participation of Kcnq4, a key component of the delayed rectifier potassium channel. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship between Dalfampridine and Kcnq4, likely through a shared mechanism involving the modulation of potassium channel function. The evidence implies that Dalfampridine may influence Kcnq4 through a common pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of other potassium channels that are part of the same functional network. The integration of these paths highlights a potential role for Dalfampridine in regulating Kcnq4 through the modulation of potassium channel activity, which is a recurring mechanism across the evidence.",
